The PE build links with -flto=thin. Two kinds of file cannot go through it.

Sources that define or refer to symbols from inline asm inside a function: the
LTO symbol table only reads module level asm, so the symbols are missing or
dropped and the link reports them undefined. These are the RTTI and vtable
definitions of the C++ runtime emulation, the unwind handlers of ntdll and
wow64's asm callers.

The static runtime libraries: LTO code generation emits calls to library
functions such as fetestexcept and _dsign, and lld cannot take a bitcode
archive member for them after code generation has run.

Compile all of these without LTO.

